  "responseTimeMs": 17236,
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nA VAT-registered exporter that sells 100% of its goods abroad can obtain a refund or tax credit for input VAT. This is provided under the provisions of the NIRC.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor VAT-registered exporters, this means that they can effectively reduce their tax burden by claiming refunds or credits for the input VAT they have paid on goods and services that are directly related to their export sales. This mechanism supports their competitiveness in the international market by alleviating the cost of VAT on inputs used for goods sold abroad.",
